    "problem_statement": "When a spinel property is set to an empty value (for example clearing the MAC source-match short-address list or the MAC scan mask by passing a null/zero-length data argument), the radio layer rejects the request and reports an error instead of accepting it. Setting such a property should succeed (returning success), the property should read back as an empty value (zero length), and no spinel parse error should be recorded. This affects both property Set (which packs an empty value into the outgoing command) and the response path (which unpacks an empty value), as well as the logger that unpacks data fields.",
